    transliteration: "str\u012b\u1e47\u0101\u1e43 sahasrabharai\u1e25 putravat\u012b ya\u015bod\u0101 dhany\u0101 yay\u0101 sutavaro bhavadabhyadh\u0101yi | di\u015bo'pi sarv\u0101\u1e25 phalavantyavabh\u0101sit\u0101\u015bca digdak\u1e63i\u1e47eva na tath\u0101 kakubh\u0101\u1e43 pras\u016bt\u0101 ||",
    meaning: "Many mothers have borne sons, but blessed is Mother Marudevi who gave birth to You, the jewel of sons. All directions produce common stars, but only the eastern horizon brings forth the brilliant sun.",
